WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.000
Guys, right now it is time for "Tonight Show Hashtags."

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.033
Here we go.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.300
-♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.701
♪♪

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.234
♪ Hashtags ♪

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:12.501
♪♪

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.667
-We do this thing every week where I send out a hashtag

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.734
and ask you guys to respond to that topic.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.901
So, since the new trailer for "Thor: Love and thunder"

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:23.467
came out this week -- I can't wait. It looks awesome.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.467
I sent out the hashtag #RejectedSuperheroes.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.100
And I asked you guys to share

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.801
some of your funniest ideas for a bad superhero name.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.400
Within minutes, it was a trending topic,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.801
so thank you for playing along.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.601
Now I thought I'd share

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.968
some of my favorite rejected superheroes from you guys.

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:42.234
This first one here is from @mellotron42.

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:43.868
-Ooh. -Ooh.

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.901
-What is a mellotron, James? James, that's more like --

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.367
[ Imitating instrument ]

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:48.734
Do you have mellotron?

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.968
[ Mellotron melody playing ]

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.767
-Ooh. The Beatles.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:56.067
-♪ Yeah, it's Beatle-y, it's Beatles ♪

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.701
♪ And it's John and it's Paul ♪

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:03.734
♪ And Ringo and, of course, it's George, too ♪

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.300
♪ Da, da-ba-da-da, whee ♪

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.767
Alright. That's a mellotron.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.701
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:10.934
I like that sound.

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.734
All right, so, @mellotron42.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:14.534
These are his bad superhero names.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.300
He says..."Superman Bun."

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.801
Oh, there you go.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.467
-Oh, boy.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.734
-"You mind if I crash at your place for a week?"

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.534
-Wait. That's your super power?

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:26.067
-This one is from @Ghost-7.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.501
-Ooh. -They say "The Wordler."

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.734
Oh. There you go, yeah. Interesting.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.167
-"Spoil it for you!"

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.167
This one's from @GolobAdam. He says...

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:46.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:53.200
This one's from @RyanBartholomee.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.801
He says, "The Dad Joker." Oh, there you go, yeah.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.167
That should be a character. I like that one.

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.601
Is there any good dad jokes? Have you heard any?

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:06.601
-Lately? -Yeah. Or old ones?

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.067
You got any good ones? -Oh, my God.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.868
I've got so many, I can't even remember one.

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:12.467
-I know. I'm trying to think of a good dad joke that I heard.

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.467
No, I told that already on the show.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.801
-Was it dirty? -No.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.901
-Was it filthy? -No!

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:20.501
Uh...

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.868
-Come on! One.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.834
-I'm on a seafood diet.

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:26.467
-What's that?

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:29.167
-Fish, you know, salmon.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:31.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:35.467
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:38.267
Turn it -- Little twist. Turning it on its head.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:39.534
Yeah, exactly.

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.367
-I expected you to say, "I see food, I eat it."

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:45.400
-This is from @BrigGreene. He says...

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.267
"The 'MansCaped Crusader.'"

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.667
Oh, interesting. -Oh, hey.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.200
-Caped -- Wow.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.234
This one's from @ChefDisney.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.467
-Ooh! -That's a good name.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:56.067
You can get that? -Chef Disney?

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.067
-I'm assuming, right? -You think he works at Disney?

00:02:58.067 --> 00:02:59.434
-I don't.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.067
-Do you think he's a chef?

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:02.834
-I don't think -- Chef Disney is such a --

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.501
I mean, you'd think that'd be taken up.

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:06.367
-Yeah. -By the chef from Disney.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:07.467
-Yeah.

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:08.834
-Maybe she is the chef at Disney.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.400
I have no idea. But I don't think so.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.234
-But there's no number after it?

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.601
-No, you'd think it'd be -- What, like --

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.868
-Like @ChefDisney500... -Yeah, no.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.901
The only -- Like, this is the original Chef Disney.

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:20.501
-Wow. -Wow.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.000
-Ooh la la!

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.200
-[French accent] I'm making -- Be our guest. I know.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.601
Making Mickey Mouse pancakes for over 50 years!

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:31.868
-Mwah!

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.667
-@ChefDisney. She says...

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.534
Like, give him time. He's on his way.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:42.601
He'll fight crime.

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:46.801
This one's from @JeremyIzzy1. He says...

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:48.234
Oh, there you go.

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.501
Jeremy Izzy had to put a "1" after his name.

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:54.567
Because there was already one before Jeremy Izzy.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.467
-No Chef Disney, man. -No. Chef Disney nailed it.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.567
-I might go do, like, @ChefDisney2.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.133
-You'd probably get a lot of followers.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.634
-Yeah, I'll pretend I'm Chef Disney.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:04.868
They won't know the difference.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.334
-I don't think this person is a chef at Disney.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.234
-Really? -I don't think you'd --

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.400
-You think Disney would go, "Don't."

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.100
-Yeah, I think Disney would say no

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.601
and I think you probably also, as the chef from Disney,

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:15.834
you would probably be like,

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:17.200
"You know, I got enough going on."

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.300
-"Yeah. I'm busy." -"I don't wanna bring my work --

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.133
Yeah, I don't want to bring my work to my...

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.000
-"I cook for about a million people a day. It's too much."

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.501
-"Yeah, I want to go on Twitter and just, like, say

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.300
what I don't like about something or..."

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.067
-Complain about Goofy.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.534
-Yeah.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.467
'Cause if you're Chef Disney, it'll get traced back to you.

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:32.567
-You'll get busted. They'll go,

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:33.801
"Hey, did you say this about Goofy?"

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.033
"Yeah."

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.133
-Yeah. -"You're fired."

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:39.501
-Our last one here is from @MylaCardero.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.367
She says "Jersey Thor."

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.567
There you have it, everybody.

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:44.033
Those are our "Tonight Show Hashtags."

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.400
To check out more of our favorites,

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.968
go to tonightshow.com/hashtags.

